From 1c55764fc5c467a2f1dd12d25fe3558991d69c33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 04:16:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(auth): preflight stale Anthropic relay receipts before
 pinned requests [daveey]

Why: a sleeping host can miss relay pulls while hub refresh revokes its old access token. Reactive recovery only runs after the avoidable first 401; auth.json mtime and launchctl kickstart acknowledgement do not prove application.

Use provider-scoped success receipts, wall-clock 2x-cadence freshness and the existing relay lock. Bound lock/command/async receipt wait to one 30s budget, fail open, coalesce failed attempts for 2x cadence (60-300s), then sync the pinned row outside the relay lock. Recheck disable after the wait. Missing receipts preserve old-producer behavior. Scope is Anthropic pinned requests, not Codex or unpinned auxiliary resolvers.

Proof: first-request real pull subprocess RED then GREEN; disable-during-wait and failed-attempt backoff RED then GREEN. Canonical 8-file regression: 1545 passed, 1 skipped. Fourteen guard mutations killed. scripts/check all 21 checks passed; account-usage compatibility pins unchanged. Producer ordering contract delivered separately in state PR3532.
